  "summary_en": "Consolidated Finnish Aviation Act governing civil, military and state aviation: aircraft registration, airworthiness, licensing, aerodromes, security. It includes unmanned aircraft provisions: UAS airspace zones, U-space airspace, market surveillance, remote pilots, and links to EU drone regulations 2019/947 and 2019/945.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Traficom is the national aviation authority and market surveillance body for unmanned aircraft systems.",
   "Traficom may establish UAS airspace zones restricting or exempting drone operations, for up to three years.",
   "Traficom may establish U-space airspace where drones operate only with U-space services.",
   "Aircraft require registration, airworthiness certificates, and approved design, production and maintenance.",
   "Remote pilots need licences and medical certificates; remote pilot stations must be safely crewed."
  ],
